@startuml cgms_fta
title Fault Tree Analysis – Incorrect Glucose Value

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "Incorrect\nGlucose Value\nPresented to User" as TOP

' --------------------
' Level 1 Causes
' --------------------
component "Sensor Degradation" as S1
component "Signal Processing Failure" as S2
component "Lifecycle / Expiration Failure" as S3
component "Power-Related Failure" as S4
component "Data Validation Failure" as S5

TOP --> S1
TOP --> S2
TOP --> S3
TOP --> S4
TOP --> S5

' --------------------
' Sensor Degradation
' --------------------
component "Enzyme Degradation" as S1a
component "Electrode Fouling" as S1b
component "Temperature Out-of-Range" as S1c

S1 --> S1a
S1 --> S1b
S1 --> S1c

' --------------------
' Signal Processing
' --------------------
component "ADC Saturation" as S2a
component "Excess Noise" as S2b
component "Temperature Compensation Error" as S2c

S2 --> S2a
S2 --> S2b
S2 --> S2c

' --------------------
' Lifecycle / Expiration
' --------------------
component "Wear-Time Exceeded\nBut Measurement Allowed" as S3a
component "Expired Sensor\nNot Invalidated" as S3b

S3 --> S3a
S3 --> S3b

' --------------------
' Power-Related
' --------------------
component "Low Battery\nDuring Sampling" as S4a
component "Brownout Affecting ADC" as S4b

S4 --> S4a
S4 --> S4b

' --------------------
' Validation / Diagnostics
' --------------------
component "Diagnostics Missed Fault" as S5a
component "Quality Flag Incorrect" as S5b
component "Invalid Data Sent Over BLE" as S5c

S5 --> S5a
S5 --> S5b
S5 --> S5c

' --------------------
' Mitigations
' --------------------
note bottom of TOP
Implemented Risk Controls:
- Factory calibration only
- Sensor wear-time enforcement
- Power-aware sampling
- Diagnostics + fault escalation
- Quality / validity gating
- No BLE exposure of invalid data
end note

@enduml
